1
00:00:00,841 --> 00:00:02,634
[door opens, closes]

2
00:00:02,718 --> 00:00:03,927
[Chinatsu] Good morning.

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,013
Good morning to you.

4
00:00:07,222 --> 00:00:08,765
You're up early as usual.

5
00:00:08,849 --> 00:00:10,308
Yep, a new term's starting.

6
00:00:10,976 --> 00:00:13,395
Whoa, you've got bedhead.
Like, right here.

7
00:00:13,478 --> 00:00:14,438
What?

8
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:15,814
[Taiki grunts]

9
00:00:16,982 --> 00:00:18,275
We must look stupid!

10
00:00:21,445 --> 00:00:24,239
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>It seems like
ever since we went to the beach,</i>

11
00:00:24,322 --> 00:00:27,367
{\an8}<i>that awkward feeling between
Chinatsu and me has disappeared.</i>

12
00:00:27,451 --> 00:00:28,452
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

13
00:00:28,535 --> 00:00:32,539
<i>Nothing's really changed.
I still like Chinatsu.</i>

14
00:00:32,622 --> 00:00:35,167
<i>She's still putting everything
into basketball,</i>

15
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,210
<i>and living at my house
so she can keep playing.</i>

16
00:00:38,336 --> 00:00:41,965
<i>But even more than before,
it's like we're...</i>

17
00:00:42,883 --> 00:00:44,885
[opening theme song playing]

18
00:01:09,242 --> 00:01:12,662
BLUE BOX

19
00:02:12,013 --> 00:02:12,931
CULTURAL FESTIVAL

20
00:02:13,014 --> 00:02:15,934
{\an8}[Niina] It's been decided that our class
will put on the play <i>Snow White,</i>

21
00:02:16,017 --> 00:02:17,853
{\an8}with our own Hina Chono as the lead!

22
00:02:17,936 --> 00:02:18,979
{\an8}EPISODE 16
UNFAIR WOMAN

23
00:02:19,062 --> 00:02:20,438
{\an8}- It's gonna be a smash.
- [clapping]

24
00:02:20,522 --> 00:02:23,108
Never fear! You're all safe aboard my ark!

25
00:02:23,191 --> 00:02:24,901
- Your ark?
- [Hina] Don't ya get it?

26
00:02:24,985 --> 00:02:27,195
Can she even memorize lines?

27
00:02:27,279 --> 00:02:29,823
She's certainly used to
performing for an audience.

28
00:02:31,491 --> 00:02:33,702
Huh? Taiki!

29
00:02:34,536 --> 00:02:35,829
You're the class representative,

30
00:02:35,912 --> 00:02:38,290
so you need to be a leader,
and keep us in line!

31
00:02:38,373 --> 00:02:41,084
Sure, I'm the class rep,
but I just take care of the small stuff.

32
00:02:42,085 --> 00:02:44,588
Shimazaki's in charge. She's the director.

33
00:02:44,671 --> 00:02:47,340
[Hina] What are you talking about?
Don't put it all on Niina.

34
00:02:47,424 --> 00:02:51,261
You have to make sure everything stays
on track, even when we run into problems.

35
00:02:51,344 --> 00:02:53,346
Then don't cause problems
in the first place.

36
00:02:54,389 --> 00:02:56,558
I mean, obviously I'm excited.

37
00:02:56,641 --> 00:02:58,977
To the extent that I'm able,
I'll be happy to help out.

38
00:03:01,021 --> 00:03:01,980
[Yoshiki] Inomata!

39
00:03:03,106 --> 00:03:04,733
Here's the program for our play.

40
00:03:04,816 --> 00:03:06,985
Can you turn it in
to the second-year chair?

41
00:03:09,821 --> 00:03:10,739
Sure thing.

42
00:03:11,823 --> 00:03:12,949
Be back later.

43
00:03:13,033 --> 00:03:14,659
There goes our worker bee.

44
00:03:15,368 --> 00:03:17,746
Maybe this role is part
of his fitness training.

45
00:03:19,873 --> 00:03:20,874
[Kyo] Hm.

46
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:22,751
So, hey.

47
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,087
It's not like Taiki said anything to me...

48
00:03:26,171 --> 00:03:28,632
You told him, though... that you like him?

49
00:03:28,715 --> 00:03:30,842
- What!
- [girl] You are so loud.

50
00:03:30,926 --> 00:03:33,720
[Hina] Uh, just a vocal exercise.

51
00:03:33,803 --> 00:03:34,763
You okay?

52
00:03:34,846 --> 00:03:35,972
[Hina sighs]

53
00:03:36,973 --> 00:03:40,352
Taiki has feelings for Chinatsu,
and they live together.

54
00:03:40,435 --> 00:03:42,979
Oh. Well, aren't you the nosy one.

55
00:03:43,063 --> 00:03:45,899
- Wait are you worried about me?
- I'm not.

56
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:48,151
'Cause that's just how it is!

57
00:03:48,235 --> 00:03:50,946
- [Kyo] Hm?
- I realized I like Taiki,

58
00:03:51,029 --> 00:03:52,530
and that's all there is to it!

59
00:03:53,406 --> 00:03:54,282
[Niina] Hina!

60
00:03:55,116 --> 00:03:56,284
[Hina] Coming!

61
00:03:57,369 --> 00:04:00,038
[Kyo] <i>Still, it can't be easy for her.</i>

62
00:04:03,041 --> 00:04:04,292
[knocking at door]

63
00:04:04,376 --> 00:04:06,294
Excuse me. Anyone here?

64
00:04:09,631 --> 00:04:11,758
- [Chinatsu] Taiki.
- [grunts softly]

65
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:13,301
Something happen?

66
00:04:14,010 --> 00:04:16,805
I stopped by to turn in
our program to Sasaki.

67
00:04:16,888 --> 00:04:21,184
Oh, gotcha. Well, everyone's out preparing
for the Cultural Festival right now.

68
00:04:21,268 --> 00:04:22,769
I could turn it in?

69
00:04:22,852 --> 00:04:24,145
Yes, that'd be great.

70
00:04:25,021 --> 00:04:28,400
- Are you gonna come in?
- Ah. Oh, right, excuse me.

71
00:04:29,276 --> 00:04:31,695
[Taiki] <i>Entering a second-year classroom
freaks me out.</i>

72
00:04:32,487 --> 00:04:34,823
You have a great spot in here, Chinatsu.

73
00:04:34,906 --> 00:04:37,075
By the window, and in the back.

74
00:04:37,158 --> 00:04:39,160
We just redid the seating chart.

75
00:04:39,744 --> 00:04:42,414
It's a new semester, so did we.

76
00:04:42,497 --> 00:04:44,457
So then where is your spot?

77
00:04:44,541 --> 00:04:46,167
[grunts] Uh...

78
00:04:47,419 --> 00:04:48,753
Actually, here.

79
00:04:48,837 --> 00:04:50,171
That's too bad.

80
00:04:50,255 --> 00:04:51,715
Why, what makes you say that?

81
00:04:51,798 --> 00:04:55,093
'Cause if we were in the same year,
we'd sit next to each other.

82
00:04:58,805 --> 00:05:01,808
It's only because you didn't wait
one more year to be born.

83
00:05:02,434 --> 00:05:04,811
Then you could've let me
copy your homework.

84
00:05:04,894 --> 00:05:06,354
Do your own homework!

85
00:05:07,939 --> 00:05:10,150
You know, you sit in the back,

86
00:05:10,233 --> 00:05:12,444
but don't seem like
you'd sleep during class.

87
00:05:12,527 --> 00:05:14,612
Yep. No sleeping here.

88
00:05:17,198 --> 00:05:20,243
<i>But you seem like one
who'd sleep during class, Taiki.</i>

89
00:05:20,327 --> 00:05:22,412
<i>And when you'd be up next
to answer a question,</i>

90
00:05:22,495 --> 00:05:24,998
<i>you'd stay asleep
even when I'd try to wake you.</i>

91
00:05:25,081 --> 00:05:26,875
All right, next up. Inomata.

92
00:05:27,417 --> 00:05:28,251
Inomata!

93
00:05:28,835 --> 00:05:30,295
[yells] Yes!

94
00:05:30,795 --> 00:05:33,423
Third section under question one.

95
00:05:33,506 --> 00:05:35,008
Um, it...

96
00:05:37,302 --> 00:05:39,345
Uh... three times pi divided by four.

97
00:05:39,429 --> 00:05:42,515
Correct. Make sure
you pay attention in class.

98
00:05:42,599 --> 00:05:43,725
Yes.

99
00:05:44,476 --> 00:05:45,935
[chuckles]

100
00:05:47,729 --> 00:05:49,147
[chuckles]

101
00:05:54,486 --> 00:05:56,279
[wind blowing]

102
00:06:02,744 --> 00:06:05,413
I think you're gonna have to figure out
how to skip a grade, then.

103
00:06:05,497 --> 00:06:06,998
There's no way!

104
00:06:07,082 --> 00:06:08,291
I'm joking.

105
00:06:09,084 --> 00:06:10,168
Kano!

106
00:06:10,752 --> 00:06:12,420
I think I'm gonna head back.

107
00:06:12,504 --> 00:06:14,422
Okay. I'll pass this on.

108
00:06:15,507 --> 00:06:17,801
[Taiki] <i>If I could skip a grade, I would.</i>

109
00:06:18,885 --> 00:06:20,929
<i>From the beginning,
we've been in different grades,</i>

110
00:06:21,012 --> 00:06:22,514
<i>played different sports.</i>

111
00:06:22,597 --> 00:06:25,183
<i>And all I could do
was stare at her through the net.</i>

112
00:06:27,685 --> 00:06:31,064
<i>This just reminds me that we
wouldn't have gotten to know each other</i>

113
00:06:31,147 --> 00:06:33,066
<i>if we hadn't lived together.</i>

114
00:06:33,858 --> 00:06:35,902
- [Taiki] I'm home.
- [Yukiko] That must've been hard.

115
00:06:35,985 --> 00:06:37,445
[Taiki] <i>Someone's here.</i>

116
00:06:37,529 --> 00:06:39,864
- [Yukiko] I'm sorry to trouble you.
- Hey, everyone.

117
00:06:39,948 --> 00:06:43,201
- Huh?
- Hi there, Taiki! Long time no see!

118
00:06:43,284 --> 00:06:45,787
Chinatsu's mom? What are you doing here?

119
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:47,080
You're back in Japan?

120
00:06:47,163 --> 00:06:49,749
Chinatsu's grandpa collapsed
the other day,

121
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:51,835
I hopped on a plane as soon as I could.

122
00:06:51,918 --> 00:06:54,212
What? Is he going to be all right?

123
00:06:54,796 --> 00:06:56,881
He'll live, if that's what you're asking,

124
00:06:56,965 --> 00:06:59,551
but he has surgery
scheduled for next month.

125
00:06:59,634 --> 00:07:01,636
So I'm thinking of renting
a furnished apartment

126
00:07:01,719 --> 00:07:04,264
- month-to-month for a while.
- Oh, I see.

127
00:07:04,848 --> 00:07:10,186
That's why Chinatsu will be going
to live with her mom for the time being.

128
00:07:10,270 --> 00:07:11,438
What?

129
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,816
[Chinatsu's mom] Thank you, Taiki.

130
00:07:14,899 --> 00:07:18,069
It was very nice of you
to help carry all our luggage.

131
00:07:18,153 --> 00:07:19,320
No worries.

132
00:07:20,113 --> 00:07:23,074
[Yukiko] It's a good thing you found
such a nice apartment month-to-month.

133
00:07:23,158 --> 00:07:24,534
Yes, we're lucky.

134
00:07:24,617 --> 00:07:27,454
Although, it's not as close
to their school as your house is,

135
00:07:27,537 --> 00:07:28,997
but we'll figure it out.

136
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:32,542
I know it's only for a month
till her grandfather has surgery,

137
00:07:32,625 --> 00:07:35,712
but we're really going to miss her.
Won't we, Taiki?

138
00:07:35,795 --> 00:07:38,715
Huh? Uh... Oh, yes, we will.

139
00:07:38,798 --> 00:07:40,842
Don't be shy now. [chuckles]

140
00:07:41,718 --> 00:07:44,179
[Taiki] I'll be waiting
for you in the car.

141
00:07:44,262 --> 00:07:47,265
Taiki... here's your key back.

142
00:07:47,348 --> 00:07:49,601
[Taiki] Uh, thank you.

143
00:07:49,684 --> 00:07:52,645
No way, I should be thanking you.

144
00:07:52,729 --> 00:07:54,105
I know practice is soon.

145
00:07:54,898 --> 00:07:57,692
And you have a practice game
at another school, right?

146
00:07:57,775 --> 00:07:59,027
Yeah, at Nishijo.

147
00:07:59,736 --> 00:08:00,737
Gotcha.

148
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:03,740
So, tomorrow. See you at morning gym.

149
00:08:04,324 --> 00:08:05,325
[gasps softly]

150
00:08:07,076 --> 00:08:10,497
[Taiki] <i>Oh, yeah.
We may not be living together right now</i>

151
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,290
<i>but we have gotten closer!</i>

152
00:08:12,373 --> 00:08:14,834
<i>We can talk at morning practice!
Same as always!</i>

153
00:08:15,627 --> 00:08:16,753
Good morning!

154
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:20,048
<i>Huh? Maybe I'm too early.</i>

155
00:08:21,758 --> 00:08:23,718
<i>She lives farther away now.</i>

156
00:08:23,801 --> 00:08:26,763
<i>- So I guess things won't be the same.</i>
- [footsteps]

157
00:08:27,347 --> 00:08:28,765
Good morning.

158
00:08:28,848 --> 00:08:31,351
Aw, man, if it isn't Haryu.
What a surprise.

159
00:08:31,434 --> 00:08:33,102
You're never here this early.

160
00:08:33,186 --> 00:08:35,772
My mom was heading out
for something and woke me up.

161
00:08:36,356 --> 00:08:38,274
[Taiki] <i>I've got a bad feeling about this.</i>

162
00:08:38,358 --> 00:08:40,860
It's pretty nice out today.
Why don't we go for a run?

163
00:08:40,944 --> 00:08:43,196
[Taiki] <i>This guy's
full of energy this early?</i>

164
00:08:43,279 --> 00:08:45,532
- And, we're going.
- Huh? Wha... Wait...

165
00:08:45,615 --> 00:08:48,785
<i>I don't mind running,
but why's it gotta be today of all days?</i>

166
00:08:48,868 --> 00:08:50,787
CONGRATS ON NATIONALS

167
00:08:51,454 --> 00:08:52,664
[groans]

168
00:08:53,581 --> 00:08:56,000
<i>I didn't get to see Chinatsu after all.</i>

169
00:08:56,793 --> 00:08:59,837
<i>I can't believe he made me
run the entire practice!</i>

170
00:09:00,964 --> 00:09:05,552
<i>It was kinda weird, though,
that Chinatsu wasn't the first one there.</i>

171
00:09:06,177 --> 00:09:07,053
[Niina] Inomata.

172
00:09:08,096 --> 00:09:10,056
Claps reps have a festival meeting.

173
00:09:10,139 --> 00:09:12,809
[Taiki] <i>I know
her living situation's changed,</i>

174
00:09:12,892 --> 00:09:14,978
<i>but she made it to morning practice,
no problem,</i>

175
00:09:15,061 --> 00:09:16,646
<i>when she moved into my house.</i>

176
00:09:17,772 --> 00:09:20,191
<i>Wait, what if she didn't come to school?</i>

177
00:09:20,275 --> 00:09:21,192
SEMINAR ROOM

178
00:09:21,276 --> 00:09:22,443
<i>Maybe she got sick.</i>

179
00:09:22,527 --> 00:09:23,945
[inaudible]

180
00:09:24,028 --> 00:09:24,946
[exclaims softly]

181
00:09:26,322 --> 00:09:27,448
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

182
00:09:28,992 --> 00:09:32,328
<i>If I didn't see her in the gym,
or run into her somewhere else,</i>

183
00:09:32,412 --> 00:09:34,706
<i>I wouldn't have known she was at school.</i>

184
00:09:35,748 --> 00:09:36,708
[gasps]

185
00:09:36,791 --> 00:09:38,167
[gasps]

186
00:09:38,251 --> 00:09:39,961
- Kano.
- [Chinatsu] Yes!

187
00:09:40,044 --> 00:09:42,213
[grunts, sighs]

188
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:44,716
[sighs]

189
00:09:45,383 --> 00:09:47,093
What's up with you?

190
00:09:47,176 --> 00:09:49,596
- [Taiki] Stomach ache.
- Oh, so you're fine, then.

191
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,932
{\an8}HOW TO SKIP A GRADE

192
00:09:53,016 --> 00:09:54,100
{\an8}[Kyo] You're joking.

193
00:09:55,268 --> 00:09:56,352
Yep. Joking.

194
00:09:57,061 --> 00:09:59,105
I guess there's no point in worrying

195
00:09:59,188 --> 00:10:02,025
about things in my life
that I have no control over.

196
00:10:02,108 --> 00:10:04,110
- [Haryu] Taiki, you're up!
- All right!

197
00:10:05,612 --> 00:10:06,613
Ready!

198
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:09,949
- [girl 1] Keep it up!
- [girl 2] Ten more seconds!

199
00:10:10,033 --> 00:10:11,868
- [Chinatsu] You got this!
- [Taiki gasps]

200
00:10:11,951 --> 00:10:15,163
- Keep going. Don't stop.
- [Taiki] <i>That was Chinatsu's voice.</i>

201
00:10:15,246 --> 00:10:18,166
<i>This reminds me
of before we started living together.</i>

202
00:10:18,249 --> 00:10:21,252
<i>Small things like this made me happy.</i>

203
00:10:22,837 --> 00:10:24,088
[rackets whooshing]

204
00:10:24,172 --> 00:10:27,634
[Coach Yuasa] All right, guys!
Time to wrap it up!

205
00:10:28,343 --> 00:10:29,802
Just a little longer.

206
00:10:29,886 --> 00:10:32,555
[Coach Yuasa] Ten, nine, eight...

207
00:10:32,639 --> 00:10:35,141
[Taiki] Roger that. We'll clean up.

208
00:10:35,224 --> 00:10:38,144
- Where's girls' basketball?
- [Kyo] They left already.

209
00:10:38,227 --> 00:10:39,771
[grunts] How'd I miss it?

210
00:10:42,231 --> 00:10:45,652
[Taiki] <i>I was hoping to see her
one more time before I went home.</i>

211
00:10:46,694 --> 00:10:48,279
<i>Today really wore me out.</i>

212
00:10:48,363 --> 00:10:50,907
<i>The morning run,
helping with the school festival,</i>

213
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:52,659
<i>then practice on top of that.</i>

214
00:10:53,576 --> 00:10:56,663
<i>I wonder if Haryu's gonna
wake up early again tomorrow.</i>

215
00:10:57,497 --> 00:11:00,667
<i>I need to fill out the
Equipment Sign-Out Form when I get home.</i>

216
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:05,546
<i>But even when I get home,
Chinatsu's not gonna be there.</i>

217
00:11:06,798 --> 00:11:08,674
<i>One whole month, huh?</i>

218
00:11:09,842 --> 00:11:12,178
<i>I'll try to talk to her more
starting tomorrow.</i>

219
00:11:12,261 --> 00:11:14,806
<i>Yeah! We're not under the same roof,</i>

220
00:11:14,889 --> 00:11:17,058
<i>so I'll find ways
to talk to her at school!</i>

221
00:11:17,767 --> 00:11:19,227
<i>And, anyway...</i>

222
00:11:19,310 --> 00:11:20,728
[wind blowing]

223
00:11:20,812 --> 00:11:23,564
<i>...this is going to become
the norm at some point.</i>

224
00:11:28,778 --> 00:11:29,695
I'm home.

225
00:11:29,779 --> 00:11:31,697
- Oh, welcome back.
- Huh?

226
00:11:31,781 --> 00:11:33,199
Why are you here?

227
00:11:33,282 --> 00:11:35,993
<i>Wait, is she staying with us after all?</i>

228
00:11:36,077 --> 00:11:37,703
Aren't you staying at the apartment?

229
00:11:37,787 --> 00:11:40,206
Yeah, but I left a few things behind.

230
00:11:40,289 --> 00:11:41,290
Oh, okay.

231
00:11:41,374 --> 00:11:44,836
And then, there was something
that I wanted to say to you.

232
00:11:45,586 --> 00:11:47,588
You weren't there this morning.

233
00:11:47,672 --> 00:11:49,173
Yes, I was!

234
00:11:50,591 --> 00:11:53,386
But, Haryu made me go on a run with him.

235
00:11:53,469 --> 00:11:54,804
[Chinatsu] Haryu did?

236
00:11:54,887 --> 00:11:57,432
[Taiki] Actually, the one
who wasn't there was you!

237
00:11:57,515 --> 00:12:00,435
[Chinatsu] Well, I got
on the wrong train by accident.

238
00:12:00,518 --> 00:12:02,353
- So you...
- But...

239
00:12:03,187 --> 00:12:05,857
I ran to school from the station.

240
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,024
[gasps softly]

241
00:12:08,443 --> 00:12:09,986
[panting]

242
00:12:19,829 --> 00:12:22,665
[Taiki] <i>I was right.
We have gotten closer.</i>

243
00:12:23,624 --> 00:12:26,544
Well, we'll try again tomorrow.

244
00:12:26,627 --> 00:12:27,795
See you then.

245
00:12:29,922 --> 00:12:33,176
[student as witch] Beautiful young lady,
I have a gift for you.

246
00:12:33,843 --> 00:12:36,512
Oh, my! What a beautiful apple!

247
00:12:36,596 --> 00:12:38,514
Its skin is so red and glossy,

248
00:12:38,598 --> 00:12:41,309
its bottom is so plump,
and its form so pleasing.

249
00:12:41,392 --> 00:12:44,520
It looks to be the sweetest apple
I've seen in quite some time.

250
00:12:44,604 --> 00:12:47,356
[student as witch] I dare say
you're right, young miss!

251
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,025
Its mellow aroma and its...

252
00:12:49,942 --> 00:12:51,027
Aroma...

253
00:12:51,110 --> 00:12:52,195
I'm so sorry.

254
00:12:52,278 --> 00:12:54,405
No, don't worry, you're doing great.

255
00:12:54,489 --> 00:12:56,324
You've done a lot in a short time.

256
00:12:57,366 --> 00:12:59,911
Hina's a lot better at acting
than I thought.

257
00:12:59,994 --> 00:13:02,455
I'm not sure about the script
we're using, though.

258
00:13:02,538 --> 00:13:05,583
Keeping your confidence while being
in front of people is a skill, too.

259
00:13:05,666 --> 00:13:07,084
[Taiki] That's true.

260
00:13:07,877 --> 00:13:10,338
The costumes you're making,
they look promising.

261
00:13:10,963 --> 00:13:14,050
Being put in a situation
where you're forced to do something,

262
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:15,927
you'll find you often get better at it.

263
00:13:16,010 --> 00:13:16,886
BRO! BRO!

264
00:13:16,969 --> 00:13:18,846
Like making things for your siblings.

265
00:13:20,181 --> 00:13:22,475
[Taiki] <i>It's great seeing everyone
giving it their all.</i>

266
00:13:22,558 --> 00:13:25,353
Does anyone here have the key
for storage room B?

267
00:13:26,312 --> 00:13:28,314
I know that Taniguchi had it earlier.

268
00:13:28,397 --> 00:13:31,108
[girl] Hey, do we have any more
packing tape? We're running out.

269
00:13:31,192 --> 00:13:32,318
I'll get it.

270
00:13:32,401 --> 00:13:35,112
- [boy] How many desks did we need again?
- It's eight!

271
00:13:35,196 --> 00:13:38,741
Oh, shoot! The safety check-up meeting
is about to start!

272
00:13:38,824 --> 00:13:41,202
- [Taiki] I can go.
- Sorry about that!

273
00:13:41,285 --> 00:13:42,370
And thank you!

274
00:13:43,454 --> 00:13:45,873
[girl] Inomata's more reliable
than you'd expect!

275
00:13:45,957 --> 00:13:48,209
{\an8}He always gets to things right away,

276
00:13:48,292 --> 00:13:50,711
{\an8}and he's easy to talk to, it's so helpful.

277
00:13:51,504 --> 00:13:52,463
[chuckles softly]

278
00:13:53,464 --> 00:13:55,383
Make sure to review evacuation routes.

279
00:13:55,466 --> 00:13:56,425
SCHOOL STORE

280
00:13:56,509 --> 00:13:59,887
[Taiki] <i>Packing tape, and I guess
I'll get some permanent markers, too.</i>

281
00:14:01,597 --> 00:14:02,765
[both gasp]

282
00:14:02,848 --> 00:14:04,267
Well, good morning.

283
00:14:04,350 --> 00:14:05,268
Good morning...

284
00:14:05,351 --> 00:14:08,396
Wait, we already did this
at practice earlier.

285
00:14:09,647 --> 00:14:12,525
I felt like "good morning"
was appropriate since it's you.

286
00:14:13,150 --> 00:14:14,277
Hm?

287
00:14:15,027 --> 00:14:16,487
What was your class doing?

288
00:14:16,571 --> 00:14:17,822
It's a cafe, right?

289
00:14:17,905 --> 00:14:21,409
Yeah. We're going all out
with the outfits for the waitresses!

290
00:14:22,618 --> 00:14:24,161
There are waitresses?

291
00:14:24,245 --> 00:14:25,746
Welcome to our cafe!

292
00:14:26,998 --> 00:14:28,332
[Taiki] <i>That'd be awesome,</i>

293
00:14:28,416 --> 00:14:31,502
<i>but I don't wanna see her serving
other people in that outfit.</i>

294
00:14:31,586 --> 00:14:34,422
The thing is,
since I'm the class representative,

295
00:14:34,505 --> 00:14:36,340
I won't be serving the customers.

296
00:14:36,424 --> 00:14:37,258
Huh?

297
00:14:37,341 --> 00:14:39,677
[Taiki] <i>Never mind, I wish
I could see her in that outfit!</i>

298
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:43,264
And then your class
is doing <i>Snow White,</i> right?

299
00:14:43,347 --> 00:14:44,932
With Hina as the lead?

300
00:14:45,016 --> 00:14:46,267
That's right.

301
00:14:46,350 --> 00:14:49,812
But since I'm overseeing everything,
I won't be acting in it.

302
00:14:49,896 --> 00:14:53,065
Huh? I thought you'd be playing
Prince Charming.

303
00:14:53,149 --> 00:14:55,902
I couldn't!
I wouldn't be any good at that!

304
00:14:55,985 --> 00:14:58,321
Prince Charming
is being played by a tall girl!

305
00:14:58,404 --> 00:14:59,739
Okay, I see.

306
00:15:00,907 --> 00:15:02,617
Oh, there you are, Taiki.

307
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,702
Our teacher was looking for...

308
00:15:04,785 --> 00:15:05,620
Oh.

309
00:15:06,203 --> 00:15:07,204
Hello, Chinatsu.

310
00:15:07,788 --> 00:15:08,831
Hi, Hina.

311
00:15:09,332 --> 00:15:12,209
- Okay, well, good luck, then.
- Yeah, you, too, good luck.

312
00:15:15,421 --> 00:15:16,547
[Taiki] So, what's up?

313
00:15:16,631 --> 00:15:18,716
[Hina] We don't have enough supplies
or something.

314
00:15:18,799 --> 00:15:20,551
These and... this.

315
00:15:20,635 --> 00:15:21,719
We need all these?

316
00:15:23,512 --> 00:15:26,098
[Chinatsu's mom]
Chinatsu, the bath is all yours.

317
00:15:26,182 --> 00:15:27,475
Okay, thanks.

318
00:15:28,142 --> 00:15:30,019
<i>Koyuki, you knew, didn't you?</i>

319
00:15:30,102 --> 00:15:32,521
<i>You knew that I have a crush on Kumai.</i>

320
00:15:32,605 --> 00:15:34,982
<i>And yet, you went
on a business trip together!</i>

321
00:15:35,691 --> 00:15:37,735
<i>It was work,
there was nothing I could do about it.</i>

322
00:15:37,818 --> 00:15:40,071
<i>You think that I don't understand that?</i>

323
00:15:40,154 --> 00:15:41,906
<i>But that isn't the point!</i>

324
00:15:41,989 --> 00:15:44,241
<i>I'm talking about
how you're being with me, Koyuki!</i>

325
00:15:44,325 --> 00:15:47,578
- Koyuki really is an unfair woman.
- Hm?

326
00:15:47,662 --> 00:15:50,665
You can't argue with someone
who uses work as an excuse.

327
00:15:50,748 --> 00:15:54,168
If I had to guess, I'd bet she's probably
been leading him on the whole time.

328
00:15:54,251 --> 00:15:55,211
[Chinatsu] Mm.

329
00:15:55,294 --> 00:15:56,587
If she really wasn't interested,

330
00:15:56,671 --> 00:15:59,966
there are all kinds of ways she could have
created some distance between them.

331
00:16:00,049 --> 00:16:04,387
Everyone has their own way of pursuing
romantic relationships, obviously,

332
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:07,765
but being indecisive
and leading people on is pretty unfair.

333
00:16:08,391 --> 00:16:10,393
Right, hon? Don't you think so?

334
00:16:11,769 --> 00:16:12,645
Mm-hm.

335
00:16:14,230 --> 00:16:16,941
[Chinatsu] <i>Mom bought this rubber ducky
as a souvenir.</i>

336
00:16:19,485 --> 00:16:22,405
I am being kinda unfair, aren't I?

337
00:16:23,656 --> 00:16:24,824
I am.

338
00:16:24,907 --> 00:16:27,118
Even when I know Hina likes Taiki.

339
00:16:28,953 --> 00:16:30,413
I want to go somewhere.

340
00:16:31,205 --> 00:16:32,498
[sighs]

341
00:16:33,708 --> 00:16:38,421
<i>If I were Hina, I wouldn't want me
saying that kind of thing to him.</i>

342
00:16:41,590 --> 00:16:42,800
<i>But...</i>

343
00:16:44,385 --> 00:16:45,803
<i>at that time...</i>

344
00:16:48,764 --> 00:16:51,225
<i>the two of them weren't dating yet.</i>

345
00:16:59,150 --> 00:17:00,443
[groans]

346
00:17:05,448 --> 00:17:06,323
<i>But...</i>

347
00:17:07,575 --> 00:17:10,453
<i>when I feel like I need someone
to be there for me...</i>

348
00:17:12,955 --> 00:17:14,707
- [boy 1] Inomata!
- [boy 2] Inomata!

349
00:17:15,249 --> 00:17:16,208
{\an8}Right here!

350
00:17:16,792 --> 00:17:19,211
<i>So this is what it means
to be up to your ears in work.</i>

351
00:17:19,795 --> 00:17:21,714
[Taiki panting]

352
00:17:21,797 --> 00:17:24,216
Geez, I'm sorry I'm so late.

353
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:27,720
You look worn out.
We're playing doubles right now, though.

354
00:17:27,803 --> 00:17:29,305
[gulping loudly]

355
00:17:29,388 --> 00:17:31,140
[Taiki] I'll just drink some water.

356
00:17:32,308 --> 00:17:33,350
Ah!

357
00:17:33,434 --> 00:17:35,853
<i>I knew what I was signing up for, but wow.</i>

358
00:17:35,936 --> 00:17:38,689
<i>I don't want to practice
any less than I usually do,</i>

359
00:17:38,773 --> 00:17:40,483
<i>but I have all the prep for the festival.</i>

360
00:17:41,192 --> 00:17:43,861
Taiki, I know that it's difficult.

361
00:17:43,944 --> 00:17:44,945
Nishida?

362
00:17:45,488 --> 00:17:48,866
Indeed, time flies, and you can't
get it back once you've spent it.

363
00:17:49,492 --> 00:17:52,620
However, you've had a role
bestowed upon you,

364
00:17:52,703 --> 00:17:56,165
so you must continue to fight your battle
within what is possible,

365
00:17:57,041 --> 00:17:58,375
until the very end.

366
00:17:59,126 --> 00:18:02,797
And my role in this is
to help an underclassman

367
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,757
get as much practice in as they like.

368
00:18:06,050 --> 00:18:08,302
Okay... Nishida.

369
00:18:08,803 --> 00:18:09,762
Captain!

370
00:18:09,845 --> 00:18:12,348
- [laughing]
- Nishida's laying it on pretty thick

371
00:18:12,431 --> 00:18:14,975
since the seniors retired
and he became captain.

372
00:18:15,059 --> 00:18:17,770
We all liked him
'cause he was so laid back.

373
00:18:17,853 --> 00:18:20,022
- Good luck, Vice-Captain.
- [Haryu] Not my problem.

374
00:18:20,106 --> 00:18:23,234
[Nishida] Whom amongst you
used the term "laid back" just now?

375
00:18:23,317 --> 00:18:25,027
[boy] This act is weirding me out.

376
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:28,906
- [Taiki] Use your elbow more.
- [boy] Like this?

377
00:18:28,989 --> 00:18:31,659
I get it now. Thanks, Mr. Inomata.

378
00:18:31,742 --> 00:18:33,911
- Appreciate it.
- Yeah, you're welcome.

379
00:18:33,994 --> 00:18:35,663
Oh, Mr. Inomata.

380
00:18:36,247 --> 00:18:37,414
What is it?

381
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,208
Junior high?

382
00:18:39,291 --> 00:18:41,043
Yeah, first-year badminton.

383
00:18:41,127 --> 00:18:42,419
Needed some help.

384
00:18:42,503 --> 00:18:44,547
It's nice having
both schools combined, right?

385
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:46,215
Mr. Inomata.

386
00:18:46,298 --> 00:18:48,259
You seem to like calling me that.

387
00:18:48,342 --> 00:18:52,096
Uh, I just thought you really looked
the part of the upperclassman.

388
00:18:52,179 --> 00:18:55,057
Well, first-years are still pretty short,
that's for sure.

389
00:18:55,141 --> 00:18:57,309
But when you were
in your first year of middle school,

390
00:18:57,393 --> 00:18:59,145
you were probably his height, too.

391
00:18:59,228 --> 00:19:00,938
You wouldn't know how tall I was then.

392
00:19:01,021 --> 00:19:02,189
[Chinatsu grunts]

393
00:19:02,273 --> 00:19:03,941
[Taiki] <i>Wait. She got serious.</i>

394
00:19:04,024 --> 00:19:07,069
And anyway, I'm gonna get a lot taller.

395
00:19:07,153 --> 00:19:10,197
In the future,
I plan to grow to be about this tall.

396
00:19:10,281 --> 00:19:11,407
No fair.

397
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:14,034
I think I've just about
stopped growing already.

398
00:19:14,118 --> 00:19:15,661
Privilege of being a guy.

399
00:19:16,370 --> 00:19:18,539
I'm gonna widen the gap before long!

400
00:19:18,622 --> 00:19:19,582
[Chinatsu sighs]

401
00:19:20,541 --> 00:19:21,959
[Taiki exclaims]

402
00:19:26,046 --> 00:19:28,716
I think the height you are is perfect.

403
00:19:28,799 --> 00:19:30,384
Oh... 'kay.

404
00:19:30,926 --> 00:19:33,345
Or I'd say maybe this tall.

405
00:19:33,429 --> 00:19:36,056
Wouldn't that mean
that I've stopped growing, then, though?

406
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:37,266
[laughs]

407
00:19:37,349 --> 00:19:38,809
[Taiki] <i>Don't laugh at that.</i>

408
00:19:40,144 --> 00:19:43,772
<i>At this height,
I'm certainly closer to her face, but...</i>

409
00:19:44,398 --> 00:19:46,650
As a man, I'd like to be a bit taller.

410
00:19:48,068 --> 00:19:50,112
"The seven dwarfs said to me."

411
00:19:50,196 --> 00:19:52,031
"'Make sure to be careful...'"

412
00:19:53,199 --> 00:19:54,241
"Careful..."

413
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:58,495
"And no matter who may come here,
you must not open the door."

414
00:19:58,579 --> 00:19:59,580
Isn't that it?

415
00:19:59,663 --> 00:20:00,998
You have good memory.

416
00:20:01,081 --> 00:20:03,667
I hear the rehearsals while I'm sewing.

417
00:20:03,751 --> 00:20:06,337
You should've been
one of our actors, too, Kyo.

418
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:09,298
No way, I'm not good
with romantic stories at all.

419
00:20:09,381 --> 00:20:11,008
You do kinda give off that vibe.

420
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:14,094
Snow White has to deal
with misfortune and struggle,

421
00:20:14,178 --> 00:20:16,222
so I empathize with her.

422
00:20:16,305 --> 00:20:18,891
But marrying a prince
who shows up out of nowhere,

423
00:20:18,974 --> 00:20:20,517
I don't understand at all.

424
00:20:21,352 --> 00:20:22,519
[Hina] Hm.

425
00:20:23,187 --> 00:20:25,231
- That's very feminist.
- Hm?

426
00:20:25,314 --> 00:20:28,192
I guess we've never talked
about this before, but...

427
00:20:28,275 --> 00:20:29,944
is there anyone you like?

428
00:20:30,027 --> 00:20:31,570
What are you asking for?

429
00:20:31,654 --> 00:20:33,948
You always give advice as an outsider,

430
00:20:34,031 --> 00:20:35,991
I just wondered how it was for you.

431
00:20:36,075 --> 00:20:37,034
[Kyo sighs]

432
00:20:37,117 --> 00:20:38,535
[Hina] Mm.

433
00:20:42,623 --> 00:20:43,999
Right now, nobody.

434
00:20:44,083 --> 00:20:45,084
"Right now"?

435
00:20:45,167 --> 00:20:48,087
She going out with someone,
so I gave up on her.

436
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:50,422
Mm. Sorry.

437
00:20:50,506 --> 00:20:51,423
It's okay.

438
00:20:53,008 --> 00:20:55,928
That's why when I see you
going after somebody like Taiki

439
00:20:56,011 --> 00:20:58,639
who has feelings for another person,
I pity you.

440
00:20:58,722 --> 00:20:59,765
Pity?

441
00:21:01,267 --> 00:21:02,726
I'm also impressed.

442
00:21:07,189 --> 00:21:09,316
Having said that, Taiki's my friend.

443
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:12,778
I'm not gonna root for you to end up
with him or anything like that.

444
00:21:12,861 --> 00:21:14,738
Oh, come on, gimme a leg up!

445
00:21:14,822 --> 00:21:18,325
- No way. That spells trouble.
- Oh, c'mon.

446
00:21:18,409 --> 00:21:20,619
[Hina] So, who is this girl you liked?

447
00:21:20,703 --> 00:21:22,162
[Kyo] I'll never tell you.

448
00:21:22,246 --> 00:21:23,789
[Hina] Is it someone I know?

449
00:21:23,872 --> 00:21:25,916
- [Kyo] Who can say.
- [Hina groans]

450
00:21:27,293 --> 00:21:29,837
[Hina] <i>I'm Snow White,
yet somehow running errands.</i>

451
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,630
<i>Go make some copies.</i>

452
00:21:31,714 --> 00:21:32,756
GUIDANCE COUNSELOR

453
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,383
[Hina] Excuse me.

454
00:21:34,466 --> 00:21:35,384
Oh.

455
00:21:36,468 --> 00:21:37,886
Good afternoon.

456
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:39,179
Good afternoon.

457
00:21:39,930 --> 00:21:41,181
You need the copier?

458
00:21:41,265 --> 00:21:43,267
Oh. Take as much time as you need.

459
00:21:43,892 --> 00:21:46,603
Your class is putting on a café, right?

460
00:21:46,687 --> 00:21:47,646
[Chinatsu] Mm.

461
00:21:48,355 --> 00:21:49,982
Taiki told me about it.

462
00:21:54,153 --> 00:21:55,404
By the way...

463
00:21:56,989 --> 00:21:58,198
I told him.

464
00:21:58,741 --> 00:22:00,659
I told Taiki that I like him.

465
00:22:03,287 --> 00:22:04,371
[gasps softly]

466
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
